[{"id":"VRCE-1-22-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":1,"english":"And when the night had passed away, the mighty ascetic spoke to Kākutstha, lying down on a bed of leaves, O Rāma, surely has Kausalyā given birth to an excellent son! The first Sandhyā* should now be performed. Do you, O tiger among men, arise! You should perform the purificatory rites and contemplate the gods. *Brāhmaṇas have to perform their daily devotions thrice,-in the morning, at noon, and in the evening.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.809,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d9c82f431f04181be5235329cbd7821f39063f32f3c0a9a5459fc3e29ed21ab5","compact":"c1685a0d949fb87c7d2ced9830b8b3a5f04d7b26fdd26ce2041b958dc9436ba5","nasal":"c1685a0d949fb87c7d2ced9830b8b3a5f04d7b26fdd26ce2041b958dc9436ba5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":2,"english":"And when the night had passed away, the mighty ascetic spoke to Kākutstha, lying down on a bed of leaves, O Rāma, surely has Kausalyā given birth to an excellent son! The first Sandhyā* should now be performed. Do you, O tiger among men, arise! You should perform the purificatory rites and contemplate the gods. *Brāhmaṇas have to perform their daily devotions thrice,-in the morning, at noon, and in the evening.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.779,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0d76ba4a2a1c528407f988d04a97e1b296aa152f1845cadc4f0c15c3c26c71d2","compact":"97b78519cf339d02379b57c0c79dab2b5735840f4b2cb45c7b03e2fcb31ec9ec","nasal":"97b78519cf339d02379b57c0c79dab2b5735840f4b2cb45c7b03e2fcb31ec9ec"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":3,"english":"Hearing those proper words of the ascetic, those foremost of men, endowed with heroism, bathed, and, sipping water, began to recite the Gayatri. (The solar hymn of the Veda).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e81e5b3fa52124e126867203ae5cf4f434444746618b23931937698cc4d3a0ed","compact":"e9c7da4cb013e0d1ed63583736013487b527297b66b97371a56307cd0835d359","nasal":"e9c7da4cb013e0d1ed63583736013487b527297b66b97371a56307cd0835d359"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":4,"english":"And having performed these daily duties, those exceedingly powerful ones, greeting Viśvāmitra having asceticism for wealth, stood before him, with the object of starting on their journey.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.375,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c1758e9d7c00b68c10757e58b732c3279fdb59e33051dc284df16d88aa1528b3","compact":"cd5c5847fb644906c86ef1c8934bfa958e31b753b4069b9addb2c16a0d720c35","nasal":"cd5c5847fb644906c86ef1c8934bfa958e31b753b4069b9addb2c16a0d720c35"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":5,"english":"And as those ones endowed with exceeding prowess were proceeding, at the shining confluence of the Sarayū and the Gangā they bcheld a noble river flowing in three branches.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.629,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aec9edb23223c4b