anskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"13a61c40160374559f9549553f3e748863a5ce78fd99e8c18b6f2b2362a5990f","compact":"164aa60c7bb92198585430065f2884fe2a416cb0fc7cab0c60aa1e838c1dd8e2","nasal":"164aa60c7bb92198585430065f2884fe2a416cb0fc7cab0c60aa1e838c1dd8e2"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":9,"english":"At those words of theirs, that foremost of ascetics, smiling, said, Hear, O Rama, as to whom the asylum has belonged in time past.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.672,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6610f8393e9179bce79e1fa95fd859960e432f685ea5aea8f966035cedf08510","compact":"45728753851043122a353234da1b99be34474edcb1577fb0e409e4e0bc658446","nasal":"45728753851043122a353234da1b99be34474edcb1577fb0e409e4e0bc658446"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":10,"english":"Kandarpa, called Käma by the wise, was once incarnate (on earth.) And it came to pass that as that lord of the deities, Sthāņu, having performed here his austerities in accordance with the prescribed restrictions, was wending his way in company with the Maruts, that fool-hardy wight dared disturb the equanimity of his mind.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.788,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0094a34d746c079a157f82cd482e655b69c6a152d49460d0b493643a401158ee","compact":"75a1ed863debeb71c869822f4932525adf5e0538e36b116dada311f4eb65d900","nasal":"88c7340a01b9cf9c1793d641c099af57e1f3218cd520aaf3ed208f732aa51813"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":11,"english":"Kandarpa, called Käma by the wise, was once incarnate (on earth.) And it came to pass that as that lord of the deities, Sthāņu, having performed here his austerities in accordance with the prescribed restrictions, was wending his way in company with the Maruts, that fool-hardy wight dared disturb the equanimity of his mind.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"162eb7c7533fb9f8a485e2bed45bbc262ed659d4aef51fbb96c3baa3e20bcd80","compact":"c4f41bd0d062bcb92125a0a156e7fbddea6d426452436a1b22fd880ffdb0fdae","nasal":"77b80092cf97e2cf6ae80fbbf0b82887e9057afabf24278666f0a80322748350"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":12,"english":"Thereupon, O descendant of Raghu, uttering a roar, the high-souled Rudra eyed him steadfastly. And thereat all the limbs of that perverse-hearted one became blasted.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.7,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"96de0d235524a96eaf2d80665ebbe1c49162e4863eef5860ca06026d9a0a6f1b","compact":"8516312fc152f5f76ab59596d370b5bd71f19d3c977402f83e7c4a60e0b86e66","nasal":"2bc01273d2b58da322c2b5057e9d297f63324ca1e4e451f24e1ce0b66512706a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":13,"english":"And on his body being consumed by that high-souled one, Kāma was deprived of his person in consequence of the ire of that foremost among the deities.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.645,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e103ecc6621441d67da356b666536c904a916c41bc08690bb50eb5d1f4353652","compact":"2c8282d527b8e1c936c1bee1c5fe0ac2db1d8bc441d0645b89d3fd6011410433","nasal":"2c8282d527b8e1c936c1bee1c5fe0ac2db1d8bc441d0645b89d3fd6011410433"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":14,"english":"O Rāghava, from that time forth, he has become known as Ananga. And the place where he was deprived of his body is the lovely land of Anga.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8587a5cbe2a542e0cd8d8f594f382c1a7c3712ae75bbdc9439915e9a9ba6db0c","compact":"16d2f7063a040399554a10b8bfbd8a5f5ea2233d108c27e39033e282fd2c681d","nasal":"52eb5f5bddf9753ca245c6643101edc7359613cb11254332db5e96bb5557ffba"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":15,"english":"This sacred hermitage belongs to Śiva; and these ascetics engaged in pious acts, O hero, have been from father to son his disciples. And no sin touch them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4db00f09de0aa1196d898544b6954adbbdb4f1e999bbdab07a002e21953d5e40","compact":"a0f3c48ea90cb3e2029e550c3e6b82f084a8cf37deb266aaf26c238b3b429937","nasal":"a0f3c48ea90cb3e2029e550c3e6b82f084a8cf37deb266aaf26c238b3b429937"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":16,"english":"Here, O Rāma, in the midst of the sacred streams, will we spend the night, O you of gracious presence, crossing over on the morrow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b31ffc59e87ee1228b282d490bc4a894ee3bba01b65eb7fa20b750a3f2230f9d","compact":"4bafff4d46d56dd76544dc110666f6ea24e2360f2b5c6bbc127ba493033f7ac0","nasal":"4bafff4d46d56dd76544dc110666f6ea24e2360f2b5c6bbc127ba493033f7ac0"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":17,"english":"As they were conversing thus, the ascetics were highly delighted on discovering them by means of their far-reaching spiritual vision, and they rejoiced greatly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.842,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b629833997498e73982d1295acb79579fc16de1b234fd8675fbaf99639991bdd","compact":"2ce20ac370ce2cf2444306285fec21623dd751182848b6bebc7d9cb5d731a310","nasal":"2ce20ac370ce2cf2444306285fec21623dd751182848b6bebc7d9cb5d731a310"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":18,"english":"Then giving Kusika's son water to wash his feet and Arghya, and extending to him also the rites of hospitality, they next entertained Rāma and Laksmana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.889,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cbe4cbe9e3a4fbdbcb493e4ad303f8d54ad3a6b58d9a6bec6f76910c151b375b","compact":"c31dcbff05557050ad3858d280b4956685af5681796002ebf680e125cf872997","nasal":"7b265543b89d5c1efe30e98c66908554f77e87530c7b4480e3d5a4ca9318634c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-22-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":22,"verse":19,"english":"Having experienced their hospitality, they (the guests) delighted them with their talk. And then the saints with collected minds recited their evening prayers.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.456,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-23-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1022019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e43fe04d0a00008675be89d96fb82ede77c64b8bd34ae5e10f5eabc2ab467d18","compact":"68e7a6f62241c64b1bffebedd03f8640f8dda78742445b78487c37cefe0dad41","nasal":"e325c5ab05e21ba7465f441626e9f0b166221f69ad7f9e7bbb2f719e3198daae"}}]
